Remember, the castle wand will still be there
when you get there, so you do not need to
spend this one on the things you will want for
Gehennom or the ascension run (unless you
also need them right now).  Spend this wand
on surviving long enough to *get* to the castle.

Based on the number of wishes you say remain,
I assume you already had or wished for a means
of recharging.

Yes, you should save at least one of these
wishes until you find out what prize you get
from Sokoban, in case you want to spend
it on a source of reflection, which is probably
highly advisable if Sokoban doesn't give you
the amulet.  (If it does give you the amulet,
then you can choose between wishing for
MR or a bag of holding -- unless you save
two wishes so you can do both.)

Are you averse to artifact wishing?  The
Bat from Hell may blast you (because you
are not a rogue), but being chaotic I think
you would be able to wield it, and as a
priest I believe you can reach expert skill
with it (as opposed to most weapons, in
which a priest cannot achieve much skill),
and it is highly regarded as an excellent
weapon choice in Slash'em.

That leaves (not counting the one you're
saving for after Sokoban) one more
non-wrest wish.

s there a particular ring or spellbook you'd
like this early?  If you had a blessed book
of e.g. identify, would you be capable of
to usefully casting the spell at this point?

How are you doing for intrinsics?  Would
a tinning kit help with that?

Of course, magic resistance is always
good as well (though as a chaotic your
options for that are more limited than for
the other alignments).  Slash'em may
have options here that I'm not aware of.

The wrest wish is probably best spent
on a magic marker.  Assuming you have
managed to hang onto some holy water,
that and a couple of paper golems (or a
bit of judicious wetting) should allow you
to enchant up some armor and achieve
a reasonably good level of AC for this
stage of the game.

